    {
      "body": "EVIDENCE. Pearl tells the consumer that the next form will let them join JustAnswer for a low refundable amount, while the complaint alleges the service actually includes an immediate and continuing monthly subscription fee.\nLEGAL REASONING. The low refundable join-fee message is the core contradiction: it creates a one-time, low-cost impression before the consumer reaches the subscription-payment form.\nSTATED LAW. FTC Act Section 5(a), 15 U.S.C. 45(a); ROSCA Section 4(1), 15 U.S.C. 8403(1).",
